		"lore_12": "Some plates were forged to stay pressed forever — reminders of irreversible choices.",
		"lore_120": "The final crystal: the doors were only a prison while we feared walking beyond them.",
		"lore_13": "The Lantern Corridor was our evening walk back to the Door Observatory.",
		"lore_14": "The Pure Echo Seal opens only to one who leaves a trace behind and walks on.",
		"lore_15": "When I first rose on gravity, I remembered the sky was never a ceiling, but a road.",
		"lore_16": "The picture sharpens: I was never a prisoner here... I designed the locks.",
		"lore_17": "The Purple Door unfolds memory itself — showing what vanished as if still alive.",
		"lore_18": "In the Architect's Trial, I carved: 'Should I forget myself, let this riddle bring me back.'",
		"lore_19": "Every choice has two faces; one who fears seeing both is unworthy of the key.",
		"lore_20": "I conquered the Impossible Echo Labyrinth — now I know for certain I am 'The Architect', and the true journey begins!",
		"lore_21": "In my memory I saw twin keys — one for the body, one for remembrance.",
		"lore_22": "The rune stones are not heavy by chance; they are counterweights keeping the islands steady.",
		"lore_23": "Each time I summon the Echo, time pauses for seconds to let me meet myself.",
		"lore_24": "We built hidden vaults to guard our dearest memories from the collapse.",
